    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\nCaps Lock + number worked, but Caps Lock + Shift + key (move window / move to workspace) did not, and typed capital letters in a text field.\n\nCause: the layer key (Caps Lock remapped to F18) was an `hs.hotkey` bound with no modifiers. Hammerspoon matches those exactly, so with Shift already down F18 did not match, passed through to the app, and the Shift+key then typed a capital letter.\n\nFix (`hammerspoon/.config/hammerspoon/aerospace-keys.lua`): the layer is now an `hs.eventtap` that tracks F18 down/up whatever modifiers are held, swallows it, and looks the next key up with or without Shift (Cmd/Alt/Ctrl pass through). The same bindings are kept.\n\nOnly checked with `luac -p`; Hammerspoon is on your machine. To test after merging: `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`, Hammerspoon → Reload Config, then try Caps + Shift + h/l and Caps + Shift + 1, pressing Shift first and Caps first. If Shift-then-Caps still types capitals, the F18 remap itself is not applying: `hidutil property --get UserKeyMapping` should list it.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
